{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,12]],"date-time":"2025-10-12T19:39:30Z","timestamp":1760297970658},"reference-count":44,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"5","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2009,1,2]],"date-time":"2009-01-02T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1230854400000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":246,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Protein Science"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2008,5]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title><jats:p>Cyanovirin (CV\u2010N) is a small lectin with potent HIV neutralization activity, which could be exploited for a mucosal defense against HIV infection. The wild\u2010type (wt) protein binds with high affinity to mannose\u2010rich oligosaccharides on the surface of gp120 through two quasi\u2010symmetric sites, located in domains A and B. We recently reported on a mutant of CV\u2010N that contained a single functional mannose\u2010binding site, domain B, showing that multivalent binding to oligomannosides is necessary for antiviral activity. The structure of the complex with dimannose determined at 1.8 \u00c5 resolution revealed a different conformation of the binding site than previously observed in the NMR structure of wt CV\u2010N. Here, we present the 1.35 \u00c5 resolution structure of the complex, which traps three different binding conformations of the site and provides experimental support for a locking and gating mechanism in the nanoscale time regime observed by molecular dynamics simulations.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1110\/ps.083472808","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2008,4,24]],"date-time":"2008-04-24T22:58:13Z","timestamp":1209077893000},"page":"939-944","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":23,"title":["Conformational gating of dimannose binding to the antiviral protein cyanovirin revealed from the crystal structure at 1.35 \u00c5 resolution"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"17","author":[{"given":"Raimund","family":"Fromme","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Zivile","family":"Katiliene","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Petra","family":"Fromme","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Giovanna","family":"Ghirlanda","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2009,1,2]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_6_2_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1177\/095632020701800101"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0006-291X(02)02489-0"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_4_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2174\/1389557053402783"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_5_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0969-2126(02)00758-X"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_6_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.str.2004.07.019"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_7_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1093\/protein\/gzl040"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_8_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1073\/pnas.91.8.3127"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_9_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0969-2126(01)00653-0"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_10_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1021\/ja000858o"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_11_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1021\/ja004040e"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_12_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/828"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_13_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1107\/S0021889887012755"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_14_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1021\/bi0205698"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_15_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.pbiomolbio.2004.05.001"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_16_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1074\/jbc.M205909200"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_17_1","do